---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { REAL_PROOF, FREE_INCLUDES, FREE_EXCLUDES } from '../data/ladder';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Byte Digital | Barry Grottis, Christchurch NZ"
  description="Byte Digital is Barry Grottis — one person in Christchurch building websites since 2011. The free concept pipeline, custom software, and honest AI visibility work. No agency team, no outsourced work."
>
  <PageHero
    label="About"
    title="One person, building<br />since <span class='gradient-text'>2011.</span>"
    subtitle="Byte Digital is me. I build the systems I need for my own work, then turn them into services. That is the whole company, and it is why the free concept is genuinely free."
    breadcrumbs={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'About' },
    ]}
    dotMatrix={true}
    dmId="dm-about-hero"
  />

  <section class="section section-glow dm-edge-top">
    <div class="glow-orb purple top-left"></div>
    <div class="glow-orb mint bottom-right"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-content" style="position:relative;z-index:1">
        <div class="section-label">Why this exists</div>
        <h2 class="heading-accent">Most websites are bought before they are seen.</h2>
        <p>
          You pay good money for a website, and what you get is a slow, generic site that looks like everyone
          else's, ranks nowhere, and produces nothing. The problem is not that the work is bad — the problem is
          that you committed before you had seen anything.
        </p>
        <p>
          So I reversed it. Rather than asking you to trust a portfolio you have not checked, I build a working
          concept of your site from information that is already public, put it on a private link, and let you
          criticise it. Most of the value in that first version is that it shows you exactly what is wrong with
          your current online presence — which is often more useful than the site itself.
        </p>
        <p>
          I built the pipeline that produces those concepts to run my own work, so generating one costs me very
          little. That is the entire reason it can be free, and it is why I can offer it without needing to sell
          you anything afterwards.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is no team here. No account manager, no junior developer you never meet, no overseas call
          centre. If you work with Byte Digital you work with me, and if something is not right you say so and I
          fix it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section reveal" style="background:var(--bg-dark);border-top:1px solid var(--border-subtle);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-subtle)">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:40px">
        <div class="section-label" style="display:inline-flex">The honest numbers</div>
        <h2 class="section-title" style="margin:10px auto 0">What is <span class="gradient-text">actually true</span></h2>
        <p class="section-subtitle" style="margin:0 auto">
          Every figure on this site is one you could check. No percentages, no industry averages, no invented outcomes.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:20px">
        {REAL_PROOF.map((item) => (
          <div class="glass" style="padding:26px 22px;border-radius:16px;text-align:center">
            <div style="font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;font-size:32px;font-weight:700;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#8B78E6,#5EEAD4);-webkit-background-clip:text;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent;background-clip:text;line-height:1">{item.value}</div>
            <div style="margin-top:10px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:#fff">{item.label}</div>
            <p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--text-muted)">{item.detail}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p style="text-align:center;margin:28px auto 0;max-width:680px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-muted)">
        What is <em>not</em> on that list: client testimonials, case study results, years of "team experience",
        or a success rate. I have not done paid client work yet, and inventing those would be the easiest way to
        look more impressive than I am.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Divider />

  <section class="section reveal">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="founder-intro-card glass">
        <div class="founder-intro-grid">
          <div class="founder-intro-image">
            <img src="/images/founder.jpg" alt="Barry Grottis, founder and lead developer at Byte Digital" />
            <div class="founder-intro-glow"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="founder-intro-content">
            <div class="founder-intro-label">The person</div>
            <h3 class="founder-intro-name">Barry Grottis</h3>
            <p class="founder-intro-subtitle">Founder &amp; Lead Developer</p>
            <p class="founder-intro-text">
              I have been building websites since 2011. That has meant watching the web move from static pages
              to frameworks, to the current point where customers increasingly ask an AI assistant which
              business to use rather than typing a search. Most of my work has come out of building the things I
              needed myself and then noticing other businesses needed the same thing.
            </p>
            <p class="founder-intro-text">
              That is where CookTwo came from, and it is where the website pipeline came from. I built an
              automated system to generate and check websites, because doing it by hand did not scale. Then it
              turned out the system was more useful than the sites were — so now it is the thing that generates
              every free concept on this site.
            </p>
            <p class="founder-intro-text">
              I work with businesses across New Zealand from Christchurch. If you are local, I know the suburbs
              and the market; if you are not, the work is remote and the process is identical.
            </p>
            <div class="founder-intro-badges">
              <span class="founder-intro-badge">Since 2011</span>
              <span class="founder-intro-badge">Websites &amp; hosting</span>
              <span class="founder-intro-badge">Search &amp; AI visibility</span>
              <span class="founder-intro-badge">Custom software</span>
              <span class="founder-intro-badge">Internal AI</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Divider />

  <section class="section reveal" style="background:var(--bg-dark);border-top:1px solid var(--border-subtle)">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width:820px;margin:0 auto">
        <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:40px">
          <div class="section-label" style="display:inline-flex">What I will not do</div>
          <h2 class="section-title" style="margin:10px auto 0">The <span class="gradient-text">honest limits</span></h2>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px">
          {[
            {
              t: 'No invented proof',
              d: 'I will not manufacture testimonials, awards, client names, or case study results. If a number is not real, it does not go on this site — which is why there are no testimonials here yet.',
            },
            {
              t: 'No invented statistics',
              d: 'I will not quote a bounce rate, a conversion figure, or a "53% leave after 3 seconds" style statistic to make a case. I would have to believe it was true before I said it.',
            },
            {
              t: 'No guaranteed rankings',
              d: 'I cannot promise first-page Google or inclusion in AI answers, and neither can anyone who says they can. What I can do is remove the technical obstacles and make your business information accurate and consistent.',
            },
            {
              t: 'No unpaid work dressed up as a case study',
              d: 'The concept sites on this site are demonstrations, not client work. Presenting them as projects would be dishonest, so they are labelled as what they are.',
            },
            {
              t: 'No lock-in',
              d: 'Your domain would be registered in your name and you get full access. If you ever want to leave, you can move it without my permission. I would rather earn the work than trap you in it.',
            },
            {
              t: 'No work I cannot do properly',
              d: 'This is why two of the steps on the site are labelled "in build". I would rather turn something down than take it and let you down six weeks later.',
            },
          ].map((item) => (
            <div class="glass" style="padding:24px 26px;border-radius:16px">
              <h3 style="font-size:17px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 10px;color:#fff">{item.t}</h3>
              <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--text-muted)">{item.d}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Divider />

  <section class="section reveal">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:start" id="free-recap">
        <div>
          <div class="section-label">The free concept</div>
          <h2 style="font-size:28px;font-weight:700;margin:8px 0 20px">What you get, free</h2>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:13px">
            {FREE_INCLUDES.map((item) => (
              <li style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--text-secondary)">
                <svg width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="#5EEAD4" stroke-width="2.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="flex-shrink:0;margin-top:2px"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
                {item}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="section-label" style="color:var(--text-muted)">The honest boundary</div>
          <h2 style="font-size:28px;font-weight:700;margin:8px 0 16px">What it is not</h2>
          <p style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-muted);margin:0 0 20px">
            A concept is a demonstration. Going live properly is a separate piece of work.
          </p>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px">
            {FREE_EXCLUDES.map((item) => (
              <li style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--text-muted)">
                <svg width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="2.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="flex-shrink:0;margin-top:2px"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M18 6L6 18M6 6l12 12" /></svg>
                {item}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CTASection />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    #free-recap {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
      gap: 32px !important;
    }
  }
</style>
